    fullObjection: "Sometimes heat gives useful information. Pain, attraction, and anger can point to real needs. The mistake is letting the hottest version of the need write the whole plan.",
    fullMove: "Treat the calm state as the design window. Put food in the bag before the store. Draft the apology before the fight. Set the spending cap before the auction. Make the hot self use a path that the cool self already chose.",
    fullLimit: "You are not proving purity. You are admitting that the same person has different weather inside, and some weather needs rails.",
    line: "A hot state does not ask permission before it narrows the world.",
